---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { getDictionary } from "@/i18n/dictionaries";
import { FEEDBACK_EMAIL, VERSION } from "@/content/site";
import { paths, experiments, publishedConcepts } from "@/content/graph";
import { exercises } from "@/content/exercises";
import { pageMeta } from "@/lib/seo";

const locale = Astro.locals.locale;
const t = getDictionary(locale);
// Counts come from the content itself, so this page cannot drift from what the site actually has.
const n = { paths: paths.length, concepts: publishedConcepts().length, experiments: experiments.length, exercises: exercises.length };
const meta = pageMeta(locale, "/about", t.tagline, { title: t.about.title, description: t.about.builtInPublicDesc });
---
<Base meta={meta}>
    <div class="container py-14">
      <h1 class="display text-4xl font-semibold">{t.about.title}</h1>
      <section class="mt-8 max-w-2xl border border-rule p-6">
        <h2 class="display text-xl font-semibold">{t.about.builtInPublic}</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">{t.about.builtInPublicDesc}</p>
        <dl class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <dt class="text-muted">{t.about.version}</dt><dd class="mono">v{VERSION}</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <div class="prose-math mt-10">
        {locale === "zh" ? (
          <>
            <p>LeoMath 是我一边学一边写的数学站。每一节讲一个概念，顺序基本固定：先抛出一个问题，在实验里动手看一看，再给出定义和证明，最后做几道练习。</p>
            <p>实验都直接在浏览器里跑。读线性映射时，可以拖动两个基向量，看整个平面跟着怎么变；读微分方程时，可以改初值和步长，看数值解从哪一步开始跑偏。很多结论自己动手试过一次，比只看公式记得牢。</p>
            <p>证明不会省略。直觉能帮你猜到结论，但要确定它为什么对，还得把推导完整走一遍。</p>
            <h2>现在：v{VERSION}</h2>
            <p>目前有 {n.paths} 条学习路线、{n.concepts} 个知识点、{n.experiments} 个交互实验、{n.exercises} 道练习。我一次只加一节，问题、实验、定义、证明、练习都写齐了才放上来，所以更新不会太快。</p>
            <h2>第一版：v0.1.1</h2>
            <p>第一版很小：微积分、线性代数、微分方程三条路线，线性变换、ODE 数值解、指数函数的导数三个实验，再加一个软件页。</p>
            <h2>关于我</h2>
            <p>我是 Leo，平时学数学、写数值计算的程序，也做一些工具。学到的东西、写出来的程序和做好的软件，都会慢慢放到这里。</p>
            <h2>反馈</h2>
            <p>每个知识点、实验和软件页面底部都有讨论区，登录后就能留言。发现哪里算错了、哪句话没讲清楚，或者有别的想法，也可以直接写信到 <a href={`mailto:${FEEDBACK_EMAIL}`}>{FEEDBACK_EMAIL}</a>。</p>
            <h2>许可</h2>
            <p>数学正文采用 CC BY-SA 4.0，代码采用 MIT。</p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p>LeoMath is a mathematics site I write as I learn. Each section covers one concept, in roughly the same order: a question to start with, an experiment to play with, then the definition and proof, and a few exercises at the end.</p>
            <p>The experiments run right in your browser. In linear maps you drag two basis vectors and watch the whole plane move with them; in differential equations you change the initial value and the step size and see where the numerical solution starts to drift. Trying something once with your own hands tends to stick better than reading the formula.</p>
            <p>Proofs are not skipped. Intuition helps you guess a result; to know why it is true you still have to walk through the argument.</p>
            <h2>Now: v{VERSION}</h2>
            <p>There are {n.paths} learning paths, {n.concepts} concepts, {n.experiments} interactive experiments and {n.exercises} exercises. I add one section at a time and only put it up once the question, experiment, definition, proof and exercises are all written, so updates are not fast.</p>
            <h2>First release: v0.1.1</h2>
            <p>The first release was small: three paths (calculus, linear algebra, differential equations), three experiments (linear transformation, numerical ODEs, the derivative of the exponential) and one software page.</p>
            <h2>About me</h2>
            <p>I'm Leo. I study mathematics, write numerical code and build tools. What I learn, the programs I write and the software I finish will end up here over time.</p>
            <h2>Feedback</h2>
            <p>Every concept, experiment and software page ends with a discussion section; log in to leave a comment. If you find a mistake, a sentence that doesn't explain enough, or have any other thought, you can also write to <a href={`mailto:${FEEDBACK_EMAIL}`}>{FEEDBACK_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
            <h2>Licence</h2>
            <p>Mathematical content is CC BY-SA 4.0; code is MIT.</p>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>

</Base>
